#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179548 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/id #uuid "3a28f359-71aa-5b9b-b55c-802374e6821f" :question/math-academy-id "e-8745" :question/problem "Calculate $\\nabla\\times(3\\mathbf{F} + \\mathbf{G})$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = 3x\\,\\mathbf{i} + y^2z\\,\\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}, \\quad (\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{G})(x,y,z) = 3y^2\\,\\mathbf{i} + 4z\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\times \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =∇\\times (3F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3x & {y}^{2}z & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x)]k \\\\  & =(0-{y}^{2})i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3[-{y}^{2}\\,i]+[3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k] \\\\  & =-3{y}^{2}\\,i+3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =(3{y}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =4z\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,1,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-1,1,0) & =4(0)\\,j+k=k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179550 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "e27e6735-4d50-5c26-a20d-44454ddcdef3" :question/math-academy-id "e-8931" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) =  \\langle 0, y-z, x-y\\rangle$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z) = x+y.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times \\mathbf F = \\langle 0,\\,-1,\\,0\\rangle, \n\\quad\n\\nabla f = \\langle 1,\\, 1,\\, 0\\rangle,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F)$ at the point $(-1,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F) = f \\nabla \\times \\mathbf {F}+   \\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & y-z & x-y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (y-z)]\\,i-[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (0)]\\,j+[1\\cdot (y-z)-1\\cdot (0)]\\,k \\\\  & =(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j+(y-z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x+y)⟨0,-1,0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-(x+y),0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,-2x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(-1,1,3) & =⟨(-1)-1,\\,-2(-1),\\,1-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22b1f7e6-4442-5e2a-a841-c7b32ae47e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488541} {:answer/id #uuid "58ec558c-d6f3-58e0-9b30-c9079a8514c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i-8\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488639} {:answer/id #uuid "94698b03-5cff-5cf9-93a7-70a660e8ea1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,j+5\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488769} {:answer/id #uuid "c21e913d-8c60-59fd-a2f7-ee60ea0be642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488862} {:answer/id #uuid "d05504c9-446a-5857-96c3-6d98b995534b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58ec558c-d6f3-58e0-9b30-c9079a8514c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,i-8\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488639} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2e1827e-bb95-5b76-9c80-da8e23a83f9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8edc0c0-9a3d-5546-8149-aa1e5f0446b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-105791" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (4F+G)$ at the point $(0,1,-1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=y{e}^{x}\\,i+xz\\,j+(y-1)\\,\\text{k},\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=z\\,i.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =∇\\times (4F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ y{e}^{x} & xz & y-1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{e}^{x})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x})]k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i-(0-0)\\,j+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =4(∇\\times F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4[(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k]+z\\,i \\\\  & =4(1-x)\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k+z\\,i \\\\  & =[4(1-x)+z]\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,-1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (4F+G))(0,1,-1) & =[4(1-0)+(-1)]\\,i+4(-1-{e}^{0})\\,k \\\\  & =[4-1]\\,i+4(-1-1)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,i-8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abc12917-c767-5961-875f-8b79c0ea4558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177137} {:answer/id #uuid "08afb4e5-f12f-5c39-8a4d-af1df6ce9745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i-5\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488491} {:answer/id #uuid "5c3feea7-809e-5194-b77d-2a337acc1747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i+3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488649} {:answer/id #uuid "79d18dc1-c0bb-50e7-a72e-25cf91922adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,j-2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488712} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f59412-f61c-5a93-9b03-097a20b5443f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2f59412-f61c-5a93-9b03-097a20b5443f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488901} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eade32f-b760-5926-93db-b12fa72570ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffa5f452-f601-5e92-9491-4a18ed51c649" :question/math-academy-id "q-105798" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\times (F-G)$ at the point $(-2,0,3)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=z{e}^{y}\\,i+3\\,j-x\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=2x{e}^{y}\\,i-2{e}^{y}\\,j.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ z{e}^{y} & 3 & -x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z{e}^{y})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z{e}^{y})]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-((-1)-{e}^{y})j+(0-z{e}^{y})k \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k-[2x{e}^{y}\\,i-2{e}^{y}\\,j] \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k-2x{e}^{y}\\,i+2{e}^{y}\\,j \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{y}\\,i+(3{e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-2,0,3),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-2,0,3) & =-2(-2){e}^{0}\\,i+(3{e}^{0}+1)\\,j-3{e}^{0}\\,k \\\\  & =4\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d946afe3-e15a-5a3b-bccf-4066a1ac0034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,4,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371529} {:answer/id #uuid "e814ba27-e6cb-52bf-a67e-1e30969f25f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371530} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9b6aeb-c694-5f67-8117-e8a52fea6077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371531} {:answer/id #uuid "0fcfe303-7fec-524a-a515-3dbf010f2ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371532} {:answer/id #uuid "c91bf338-2580-5896-af10-2192936368ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd9b6aeb-c694-5f67-8117-e8a52fea6077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371531} :answer-field/id #uuid "4695403e-d1fd-52dc-841a-cfd9f0c1a1da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8abe39b-bb92-55f7-bb84-89cdb536b574" :question/math-academy-id "q-105895" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨-1,0,x{y}^{3}⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=yz.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨3x{y}^{2},-{y}^{3},0⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,z,y⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(0,-1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & z & y \\\\ -1 & 0 & x{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[z(x{y}^{3})-y(0)]i-[0(x{y}^{3})-y(-1)]j+[0(0)-z(-1)]k \\\\  & =xz{y}^{3}\\,i-y\\,j+z\\,k \\\\  & =⟨xz{y}^{3},-y,z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =yz⟨3x{y}^{2},-{y}^{3},0⟩+⟨xz{y}^{3},-y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3xz{y}^{3},-z{y}^{4},0⟩+⟨xz{y}^{3},-y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4xz{y}^{3},-z{y}^{4}-y,z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,-1,2) & =⟨4(0)(2)(-1)^{3},-2(-1)^{4}-(-1),2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067e0099-a214-57d4-869c-c70c94a82c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,0,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488485} {:answer/id #uuid "675820df-6ea9-5f30-9192-0ae8291264b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488669} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa35d43-0a5c-5368-b9f4-e38bbe3647e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488681} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a645d3-a518-5b55-bd59-e07fe9e39994" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488874} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d9f5c3-101a-532e-8e93-6d12cddd64ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "675820df-6ea9-5f30-9192-0ae8291264b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488669} :answer-field/id #uuid "87266618-2882-52b8-96d1-51f6b11cd2c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f311fcaa-7f7c-50da-9066-652f1bc7fb5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105897" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x{e}^{y},z,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=x-{e}^{y}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨-1,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨1,-{e}^{y},0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(2,0,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{y} & 0 \\\\ x{e}^{y} & z & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[-{e}^{y}(0)-0(z)]i-[1(0)-0(x{e}^{y})]j+[1(z)-(-{e}^{y})(x{e}^{y})]k \\\\  & =0\\,i-0\\,j+(z+x{e}^{2y})\\,k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x-{e}^{y})⟨-1,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}-x,0,x{e}^{2y}-{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,z+x{e}^{2y}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}-x,0,2x{e}^{2y}+z-{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(2,0,-3) & =⟨{e}^{0}-2,0,2(2){e}^{2(0)}+(-3)-(2)^{2}{e}^{0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe539af-1253-5ce3-a65b-eb50ed639c52" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dcb20c5-ace4-5356-918e-a260adfc5b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488533} {:answer/id #uuid "3e626866-926c-5638-8514-10fe8911bfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-8,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488598} {:answer/id #uuid "62f0f666-5714-5bdd-ac2c-a5c2b0a1ad02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,-1,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488660} {:answer/id #uuid "67b3423e-e4b7-56ef-b64b-3bde9aa959ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,4,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488671} {:answer/id #uuid "ce34e2bd-fa56-525d-9e23-0ce1549d6ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,4,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e626866-926c-5638-8514-10fe8911bfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-8,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488598} :answer-field/id #uuid "cee411fe-3c0d-5c7d-9c42-5d9b1df29d7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c76b758-88c8-5667-93d2-dbb6a9e1da40" :question/math-academy-id "q-105956" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\sqrt{x},0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=-z.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,0,-1⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(4,1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ z & \\sqrt{x} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(0)-(-1)(\\sqrt{x})]i-[0(0)-(-1)(z)]j+[0(\\sqrt{x})-0(z)]k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\,i-z\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(-z)⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-2z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(4,1,4) & =⟨\\sqrt{4},-2(4),-\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-8,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179689 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f429709-cb4b-5319-8d2b-0858bc409e89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8564889c-292a-5e99-ac5d-ffa3f3d8123b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5i - 2j + k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178661} {:answer/id #uuid "02305ea5-f68b-5c83-8300-962012453c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i - j + k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178662} {:answer/id #uuid "08eab681-1715-57de-94d8-fe843e62627f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3i - 4j - 4k" :db/id #edb/ref 175921861